Let me understand the original code's `stringifyName`:

```typescript
function stringifyName(name: string, next: Token | undefined): string {
  if (!ID.test(name)) return quoteName(name);

  if (next?.type === "text" && ID_CONTINUE.test(next.value[0])) {
    return quoteName(name);
  }

  return name;
}
```

For `/:foo Tigers`, the next token after `foo` is `{type: "text", value: " Tigers"}`. The first character of " Tigers" is a space, which is NOT an ID_CONTINUE character. So the name won't be quoted.

