```

The issue is about the check `ID_CONTINUE.test(next.value[0])`. The `ID_CONTINUE` regex is defined as:
```typescript
const ID_CONTINUE = /^[$\u200c\u200d\p{ID_Continue}]$/u;
```

The problem is that `next.value[0]` gets the first JavaScript character (a UTF-16 code unit), but for astral (surrogate pair) Unicode characters, this would be only the first surrogate, not the full character. The `/u` flag in the regex means it should operate on full code points, but `next.value[0]` only gets one UTF-16 code unit.

